function _accrueRewards(IERC20 _rewardToken, uint256 accrued) internal {
    uint256 supplyTokens = totalSupply();
    uint224 deltaIndex;
    if (supplyTokens != 0)
      deltaIndex = accrued.mulDiv(uint256(10**decimals()), supplyTokens, Math.Rounding.Down).safeCastTo224();

    rewardInfos[_rewardToken].index += deltaIndex;
    rewardInfos[_rewardToken].lastUpdatedTimestamp = block.timestamp.safeCastTo32();
}
```
When `totalSupply()` = 0, `deltaIndex` will be 0, then `index` of this reward token will not increase. It means at this time, rewards won't be distributed to anyone. Since `rewardsEndTimestamp` of this reward token doesn't change, so this amount of rewards will be stuck in contract.
There is not any recovery function to rescue the stuck rewards in staking contract. So the amount of rewards in the time 0 supply will be lost.
