## Impact
Some of the internal functions, such as `_setDeploymentController`, do not properly handle errors and do not check the return value of the calls to other contracts. This could lead to unintended consequences and bugs in the contract.

```solidity
_setDeploymentController(_deploymentController);
```
This line does not properly handle errors and does not check the return value of the calls to other contracts.
This vulnerability could also be exploited by malicious actors to carry out attacks on the contract. For example, if an attacker can cause an error to occur in a function that manages sensitive data, they could potentially access or modify the data, leading to a breach of privacy and confidentiality.

## Proof of Concept
An attacker can create a malicious contract that returns a false value on a function call. This malicious contract can then be passed to the internal function, such as `_setDeploymentController`, which does not properly handle errors or check the return value of the function call.

As a result, the contract could continue to execute without realizing that the call to the malicious contract has failed, leading to unintended consequences.

