# Vulnerability details

## Impact
There's No access control for `takeManagementAndPerformanceFees` function, which can result in unintended users being able to take management and performance fees.

```solidity
function takeManagementAndPerformanceFees()
    external
    nonReentrant
    takeFees
{}
```
As there is no access control for the `takeManagementAndPerformanceFees` function, anyone who is able to call the function will be able to take management and performance fees from the contract. This can result in unintended users being able to drain the contract of its assets.

## Proof of Concept
Exploiting this vulnerability, an attacker will create their own contract that calls the vulnerable contract's `takeManagementAndPerformanceFees` function. Since the function has no access control, the attacker's contract would be able to call it and take the management and performance fees, even if they are not intended to be able to do so.

## Code
