}

// Vulnerable Contract
contract Vulnerable {
  function takeManagementAndPerformanceFees() public {
    // Logic to take the management and performance fees
    // ...
  }
}
```
The attacker contract `Attacker` has a functioning exploit that takes in the address of the vulnerable contract and calls its `takeManagementAndPerformanceFees` function. Since the vulnerable contract has no access control over this function, the attacker contract is able to call it and take the management and performance fees.

